---
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import { getLocaleFromUrl, getLocalizedPath, useTranslations } from '../i18n/utils';

const locale = getLocaleFromUrl(Astro.url);
const t = useTranslations(locale);
const lp = (path: string) => getLocalizedPath(path, locale);

const sidebar = [
  {
    title: 'Team Setup',
    items: [
      { label: 'Overview', href: lp('/docs/team-setup') },
      { label: 'Start the Server', href: lp('/docs/team-setup#start') },
      { label: 'Connect Agents', href: lp('/docs/team-setup#connect') },
      { label: 'Shared Sessions', href: lp('/docs/team-setup#sessions') },
      { label: 'Governance', href: lp('/docs/team-setup#governance') },
      { label: 'Monitoring', href: lp('/docs/team-setup#monitoring') },
    ],
  },
  {
    title: t('docs.common.related'),
    items: [
      { label: t('docs.sidebarTeamServer'), href: lp('/docs/team-server') },
      { label: 'API Reference', href: lp('/docs/api-reference') },
      { label: t('docs.sidebarProfiles'), href: lp('/docs/profiles') },
    ],
  },
];
---

<DocsLayout title="Team Setup Guide — LeanCTX" description="Set up LeanCTX for your engineering team in 10 minutes. Self-hosted Team Server, shared sessions, governance, and multi-agent coordination." sidebar={sidebar}>

  <p>This guide walks you through setting up LeanCTX for a team of developers. By the end, you'll have shared context across all IDEs, budget controls, and multi-agent coordination.</p>

  <h2 id="prereqs">Prerequisites</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>LeanCTX installed on each developer's machine (<a href={lp('/docs/getting-started')}>Installation Guide</a>)</li>
    <li>Docker (for the Team Server) or a Linux/macOS server</li>
    <li>Network connectivity between developer machines and the server</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="start">Step 1: Start the Team Server</h2>
  <p>The Team Server is a single binary that coordinates sessions, events, and knowledge across your team. Run it with Docker:</p>

  <div class="not-prose">
    <pre class="code-block"><code><span class="text-muted">$</span> docker run -d --name leanctx-team \
    -p 7700:7700 \
    -v leanctx-data:/data \
    ghcr.io/yvgude/lean-ctx:latest \
    serve --team --data-dir /data</code></pre>
  </div>

  <p>Or run directly from the binary:</p>

  <div class="not-prose">
    <pre class="code-block"><code><span class="text-muted">$</span> <span class="text-accent">lean-ctx</span> serve --team --bind 0.0.0.0:7700 --data-dir ./team-data</code></pre>
  </div>

  <p>Verify the server is running:</p>

  <div class="not-prose">
    <pre class="code-block"><code><span class="text-muted">$</span> curl http://your-server:7700/healthz
<span class="text-accent">{'{"status":"ok","version":"3.5.19","uptime":"2m"}'}</span></code></pre>
  </div>

  <h2 id="tokens">Step 2: Create Access Tokens</h2>
  <p>Create a token for each developer or CI system:</p>

  <div class="not-prose">
    <pre class="code-block"><code><span class="text-muted">$</span> <span class="text-accent">lean-ctx</span> team token create --scope read,write --name "alice"
<span class="text-muted">→</span> Token: lctx_t_alice_a3f8...

<span class="text-muted">$</span> <span class="text-accent">lean-ctx</span> team token create --scope read,write,admin --name "team-lead"
<span class="text-muted">→</span> Token: lctx_t_lead_b7c1...</code></pre>
  </div>

  <h2 id="connect">Step 3: Connect Agents</h2>
  <p>Each developer configures their local LeanCTX to connect to the Team Server. Add to <code>.lean-ctx/config.toml</code>:</p>

  <div class="not-prose">
    <pre class="code-block"><code><span class="text-accent">[team]</span>
server = "http://your-server:7700"
token = "lctx_t_alice_a3f8..."
workspace = "my-team"</code></pre>
  </div>

  <p>Or set via environment variables:</p>

  <div class="not-prose">
    <pre class="code-block"><code>export LEANCTX_TEAM_SERVER="http://your-server:7700"
export LEANCTX_TEAM_TOKEN="lctx_t_alice_a3f8..."
export LEANCTX_WORKSPACE="my-team"</code></pre>
  </div>

  <h2 id="sessions">Step 4: Shared Sessions</h2>
  <p>Once connected, sessions are automatically shared. Agents on the same workspace and channel see each other's context:</p>

  <div class="not-prose">
    <pre class="code-block"><code><span class="text-muted">$</span> <span class="text-accent">lean-ctx</span> session list --workspace my-team
workspace: my-team
channel: feat/auth-refactor  rev:14  agents: cursor, claude-code
channel: fix/api-timeout     rev:7   agents: windsurf
channel: main                rev:42  agents: copilot, kiro</code></pre>
  </div>

  <h2 id="governance">Step 5: Set Up Governance</h2>
  <p>Configure per-agent budgets and roles in your team profile:</p>

  <div class="not-prose">
    <pre class="code-block"><code><span class="text-accent">[budget]</span>
max_context_tokens = 200000
max_cost_usd = 5.0
alert_threshold = 0.8

<span class="text-accent">[roles]</span>
default = "developer"

<span class="text-accent">[roles.ci]</span>
scope = "read"
max_cost_usd = 1.0</code></pre>
  </div>

  <h2 id="monitoring">Step 6: Monitoring</h2>
  <p>The Team Server exposes Prometheus metrics at <code>/v1/metrics</code> and a status endpoint at <code>/v1/status</code>. Use the observatory dashboard for a visual overview:</p>

  <div class="not-prose">
    <pre class="code-block"><code><span class="text-muted">$</span> <span class="text-accent">lean-ctx</span> observatory --open</code></pre>
  </div>

  <h2>Next Steps</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href={lp('/docs/team-server')}>Team Server Reference</a> — Full configuration options</li>
    <li><a href={lp('/docs/api-reference')}>API Reference</a> — REST endpoints and SDK</li>
    <li><a href={lp('/context-os/shared-sessions')}>Shared Sessions</a> — Deep dive into session sharing</li>
    <li><a href={lp('/context-os/context-bus')}>Context Bus</a> — Event-driven multi-agent coordination</li>
  </ul>

</DocsLayout>
